; de-Bruijn ORDER discriminator: source 2 references BOTH vars in REVERSED order.
; A `references` table indexed by push-order (instead of e.v) swaps $x/$y here and
; yields (out 1 2)/(out 2 1)-style garbage or nothing.
(e 1 2)
(e 2 1)
(e 1 3)
(e 3 4)
(exec 0 (, (e $x $y) (e $y $x)) (, (sym $x $y)))
